[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-PLAN-BEADS-SNAPSHOT
TITLE: Ingest to beads freezes the plan
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: human
STATEMENT: >>>
SUPERSEDED by MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS: too strong. At ingest the plan is snapshotted immutably and execution state moves to beads.
The plan does not track progress after that point, and beads is the only thing
whose state changes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Keeps one work state rather than two, which is the sync problem that would
otherwise appear the moment both a plan and an execution engine model an
in-progress item.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Supporting the with-beads and without-beads shapes simultaneously is explicitly
out of the author's scope. The current awkward state, where the plan carries
some execution-adjacent state because beads does not exist yet, is temporary and
should not be designed around.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
